# Stamps along a path, 256x256 on paper, four rows.
# Row 1 (y 20 to 44): a dotted line from x 16 to 240 that rises at x 80 and dips at x 160, made of
# ink dots 4 px wide, 6 px apart, with no line under them.
# Row 2 (y 56 to 120): a vine, a 3 px green stroke from 16,110 up to 70,70, down to 140,100 and up
# to 240,60, with lighter green leaves on alternate sides of it, drawn over the stem. The stem is
# brushed with bristle: solid from the left end to the dip near 140,100, then broken into thin
# streaks with gaps that narrow toward the right end, where the pressure falls to .3. Pressure
# runs .9 .6 .7 .3 along the four points, so the leaves are large and far apart at the left end,
# smaller and closer at the right end, and each leaf leans away from the stem by 15 to 40 degrees.
# Row 3 left (x 24 to 96, y 154 to 226): an unfilled 2 px ink circle of radius 36 at 60,190 with
# two sets on it: 19 red dots 12 px apart around the whole circle at one even pitch, with no doubled dot and no
# gap where the circle closes at its right, and 13 blue 1 px ticks 10 px long across the ink line
# at their own even pitch.
# Row 3 right (x 120 to 240, y 150 to 212): a ridge from 120,210 to 240,194 with no line of its
# own, holding green grass tufts every 9 px. Each tuft is three thin tapered blades that stand
# upright, lean by a random -10 to 10 degrees, and vary in height from 7 to 13 px; their blades
# are dry-brushed, so they break into streaks. A solid green hill fills a closed curve through the
# ridge's four points and 240,240 and 120,240. A curve never goes past its points, so its top follows
# the ridge from 120,210 to 240,194, its sides are straight at x 120 and x 240, and its bottom is flat
# along y 240. The tufts stand on its top edge.
# The .svg target uses profile:svg: the dots, leaves, circle, and ticks stay vector paths. Only the
# vine's own brushed stroke and each tuft's brushed blades are baked to raster tiles, and the
# vine's leaves stay vector paths drawn over its tile, so the image matches the PNG.
@artboard 256x256
@target stamp/along.png
@target stamp/along.svg profile:svg

use std/brushes { bristle dry }
use std/stamps { dots ticks leaves }

def tuft h:10 tint:p.green.1
  each k in 0..3
    curve 0,0 (k-1)*2,-h*.6 (k-1)*4,-h stroke:tint,1.2 taper:0,.9 brush:dry(strength:.3) name:blade

# Upright tufts with a random lean: the frame follows the tangent, so rot:-tangent stands them up.
stamp tufts spacing:9 h:10
  tuft h*(.7+.6*rand(0 1)) at:0,rand(-1 1) rot:-tangent+rand(-10 10) name:tuft

curve 16,36 80,20 160,44 240,28 stamp:dots(tint:p.ink) name:dotted
curve 16,110 70,70 140,100 240,60 stroke:p.green.1,3 brush:bristle pressure:[.9 .6 .7 .3] stamp:leaves(tint:p.green.3) name:vine
circle 36 at:60,190 fill:none stroke:p.ink,2 stamp:[dots(spacing:12 tint:p.red.2) ticks(spacing:17 reach:5 tint:p.blue.2)] name:wreath
curve 120,210 160,196 200,206 240,194 240,240 120,240 closed fill:p.green.2 name:hill
curve 120,210 160,196 200,206 240,194 stamp:tufts name:ridge
